{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great","id":1046916,"title":"Legion TV series shows how being Mad One can be great!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-10T13:55:14-08:00","id":1046916,"title":"Legion TV series shows how being Mad One can be great!","content":"If you did not watch this TV series about Mastigos being thrown as lunatic by Sleepers to institution - leading him to becoming real Mad One mage - then you need to catch up. Like now - you will thank me later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4SZ3rMMYBLY\" data-code=\"4SZ3rMMYBLY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4SZ3rMMYBLY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T14:41:36-08:00","id":1046929,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://m.popkey.co/5e4d6c/1zQL0_s-200x150.gif?c=popkey-web&amp;p=mars&amp;i=3musketeers&amp;l=search&amp;f=.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Thanks for the tip!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T15:08:36-08:00","id":1048437,"title":"","content":"Great show! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Don't even Mad Ones have Gnosis? He seems to lack it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T23:17:41-08:00","id":1048602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1048437#post1048437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Don't even Mad Ones have Gnosis? He seems to lack it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Character can have Gnosis not knowing he has Gnosis. How other way we would have superpowerful Banishers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T23:51:14-08:00","id":1048610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1048602#post1048602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Character can have Gnosis not knowing he has Gnosis. How other way we would have superpowerful Banishers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Can they? <br /> They don't see it as a stat, but from my reading, being the knowledge/understanding of magic, Banishers have it, are aware of it, think using it to change reality is evil.<br /> Thus do Banishers target Mages and supernal magic shenanigans for destruction, and you won't have a Banisher go &quot;magic isn't real, I'm hallucinating.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T00:08:28-08:00","id":1048614,"title":"","content":"Beaing Mad One ( and normal mad ) do not prevents you from understanding reality ( having Arcana ) on instinct level. Hell, it's even why can cast spells just after Awakening - not many people will connect 'I had a real weird dream' with 'I can cast magic!' - even if starting mage character just after Awakening surely can cast spells. They just form Imago on instinctual levels, bypassing their conscious minds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T01:27:26-08:00","id":1048626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1048614#post1048614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beaing Mad One ( and normal mad ) do not prevents you from understanding reality ( having Arcana ) on instinct level. Hell, it's even why can cast spells just after Awakening - not many people will connect 'I had a real weird dream' with 'I can cast magic!' - even if starting mage character just after Awakening surely can cast spells. They just form Imago on instinctual levels, bypassing their conscious minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong, unless you're Mad then in Awakening magic is always an active effort of the will. Mages do not cast without realizing it the need for attention to detail in an imago is too great to allow it to happen by accident. They might not know that what they're doing is magic because they haven't been introduced yet to the lexicon of Mages, but they know exactly what they're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T03:27:19-08:00","id":1048649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1048626#post1048626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong, unless you're Mad then in Awakening magic is always an active effort of the will. Mages do not cast without realizing it the need for attention to detail in an imago is too great to allow it to happen by accident. They might not know that what they're doing is magic because they haven't been introduced yet to the lexicon of Mages, but they know exactly what they're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends of what you describe as 'accident' - if you are fresh Awakened, unknown if and go with 'I wish she would love me' - your Arcana <i>will</i> try to cast spell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T03:32:37-08:00","id":1048651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1048649#post1048649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends of what you describe as 'accident' - if you are fresh Awakened, unknown if and go with 'I wish she would love me' - your Arcana <i>will</i> try to cast spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it won't, unless you deliberately and consciously form an imago to try and force her to love you with magic. Whether or not you realize you're doing magic at the time is irrelevant, you know you're doing -something- and if you succeed know it's because of what you did. Your arcana don't have a mind of their own unless you go Mad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T05:19:53-08:00","id":1048683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeryes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1048437#post1048437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great show! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Don't even Mad Ones have Gnosis? He seems to lack it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you mean Wisdom?<br /> Without Gnosis there is no magic, voluntary or otherwise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T07:30:16-08:00","id":1048740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1048683#post1048683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't you mean Wisdom?<br /> Without Gnosis there is no magic, voluntary or otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not. Without Gnosis there is no supernal magic, but there's a variety of ways to get magic-esque effects. Even some that one might call magic, but the kind that isn't of the supernal, of Mages from Mage: the Awakening.<br /> Not trying to shoehorn Legion into it,but an example that comes to mind is the psionics of the Trinity Continuum, they can warp things and telekinticise(I made it into a verb :P)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> : Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> said, you know what you're doing when you're casting a spell. And you have to understand at a deep level that is how things work. Gnosis + Arcana ratings mean you <i>know</i> magic, even if you don't call it that. <br /> <br /> From the MtA setting, the protagonist could be a shiny new Proximus. And it sucks for him that he doesn't know how to deal with his curse, so his blessings overwhelm him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T07:47:04-08:00","id":1048747,"title":"","content":"1. In MtAw setting, Legion is clearly Mad - his powers are open ended and he do not grasp them ( I. E. Wisdom 0 character). <br /> <br /> 2. Spellcasting do not need consiens using Arcana - it needs Imago of spell. From spellcasting part of 2E corebook:<br /> <br /> The mage imagines each part of the spell in her mind before she casts it, envisioning the Imago of the spell. The Imago is the mental representation of the end result of the spell including all its effects and factors. Without the Imago, the mage is incapable of fully envisioning what she wants to impart into the world, her will incapable of imprinting the truth without a defined Pattern. <br /> <br /> Newly Awakened can just imagine his future with the girl she likes and wanting it - and so the spell will be cast by him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T07:57:58-08:00","id":1048751,"title":"","content":"That is a quote from the book and it's literally telling you that forming the Imago to cast a spell is a conscious effort that requires putting together all the spell factors and effects and you somehow think that casting a spell isn't a conscious effort? How do you even manage that level of dissonance? Holy shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T08:05:52-08:00","id":1048752,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure this would be a Mad One. The unfortunately named Mad are Wisdom 0 mages that have taken Obsessions to their furthest extreme. I'm not getting an obsession vibe off this character. He's trying to figure out who and what he is, sure, but that's not the same thing as an Obsession-cum-Fault. Mad Ones also seem to have people forget about their existance, as if they were a spell subject to Quiescence, which doesn't feel like the case here either. Mad Ones are also said to completely lack empathy, which this character clearly does possess. <br /> <br /> The random spell effects should move the Mad back towards their Obsession. I'm not sure what aimlessly flying objects have to do with that, other than just losing control. That could just as easily be a sign of paradox. Or, just as possible, if not more plausable, a human psychic without willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T08:13:33-08:00","id":1048755,"title":"","content":"I just read the series overview. Its all about a character who's coming to terms that the supernatural is real, that he is a &quot;mutant,&quot; and what hes' going to do with it. That's a classic example of undergoing an Awakening, not a magical character who once had control over his power losing it as they are driven to extremes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T15:47:04-08:00","id":1048974,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with MCN, rather than being Mad, I got the feeling this was a rather average mystery play awakening <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T23:08:51-08:00","id":1049159,"title":"","content":"Well, killing everyone in mental asylum by phasing them on the walls I would not count as 'average'. And Legion is clearly at <i>least</i> disturbed, literally fighting with his 'inner demons'. Nice idea on 'ghost goetia' of his friend from Asylum he killed with his powers. And he probably has <i>Split Personality</i> Condition or <i>Amnesia</i> Condition on him, maybe both. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, <i>if</i> Legion is Awakened, he clearly has Wisdom 0, as he has no control over his powers - that's why I pointed him as Mad One.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T03:49:20-08:00","id":1049212,"title":"","content":"Ehh.... You don't need to be Wisdom 0 to have low to no control over your powers. That's literally what Paradox does. Even if we try to reassess this guy as a mage*, he could just be a low Wisdom mage that releases the dox instead of internalizing it.<br /> <br /> The problem with calling him a Mad One is that he lacks a Fault. Lack of control over magic is not the defining feature of being Mad. Its the out of control obsession. Even the out of control magic serves a purpose - driving the mage towards fulfilling the Obsession. This is just out of control powers. Is David mentally disturbed? Not balanced psychologically? Absolutely. That is different from being one of the Mad. Mental disorders do not equate to the Madness as Awakening describes the phenomenon; that madness specifically relates to out of control Obsessions. Such characters, even if disturbed, qualify as some of the greatest experts in their fields of obsession; there's no such field of specialty for David.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but Legion just lacks the qualities of the Mad. <br /> <br /> * The more I learn about the show, the less I'm convinced that calling him a mage is appropriate. Gnosis literally means knowledge, and Arcana literally means secrets. Mage magic literally involves applying knowledge to change the world. There's no themes of knowlege here in relationship to David's powers. As well, becoming mentally unstable from exposure to the supernatural that you don't understand is literally embodied by how mortal Integrity works, and David's abilities are all example psychic powers; there's even a clause for losing control if you run out of willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-15-2017, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T09:20:13-08:00","id":1049323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1049212#post1049212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but Legion just lacks the qualities of the Mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>And neither is his situation anything great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T08:47:19-08:00","id":1050523,"title":"","content":"Well I'd suspect that he's a Mastigos with the voices, demons and teleporting people into walls. So, while a dangerous awakening, I wouldn't see it as being completely out of line with one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T01:03:45-08:00","id":1051408,"title":"","content":"With second episode we have Oneiros travel and Psychic Projection cast on Sympathy. I know that in series universe David is 'mutant', but his power-level and experiance he got is all about Mastigos Awakening mixed with mental ilness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:03:21-08:00","id":1051502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1051408#post1051408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With second episode we have Oneiros travel and Psychic Projection cast on Sympathy. I know that in series universe David is 'mutant', but his power-level and experiance he got is all about Mastigos Awakening mixed with mental ilness.</div> </div> </div> </div>And powerful even for mage standards, if he is indeed a fledgeling mage. Or just having an explosive growth rate. Or he <i>still </i>hasn't completed his Awakening, and he's having a power trip during his Mystery Play.<br /> <br /> Under the assumption of David's mage-hood, I'm still waiting for the inevitable huge-ass Paradox Anomaly to wreck everyone's day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:50:24-08:00","id":1051518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1051502#post1051502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the assumption of David's mage-hood, I'm still waiting for the inevitable huge-ass Paradox Anomaly to wreck everyone's day.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Yellow-eyed demon seems to be terrifying Manifestation waiting to happen. <br /> <br /> While I like the show as inspiration for the look of magic and for possible plot ideas, I just can't imagine these mutants as Mages. They don't exhibit the multiplicity of powers that even a starting Mage would have. Anyone could instantly have more abilities than David has already shown. That's the horror of Mage to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:00:11-08:00","id":1051693,"title":"","content":"Legion is capable of ALL the mutant powers. When people die near him, he absorbs their personality. His body manifests a new power appropriate to that person's psyche.<br /> <br /> \u200bHe eventually gains the ability to access all the powers of his splinter-selfs at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T15:04:15-08:00","id":1051696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WaywardPaladin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1051693#post1051693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legion is capable of ALL the mutant powers. When people die near him, he absorbs their personality. His body manifests a new power appropriate to that person's psyche.<br /> <br /> \u200bHe eventually gains the ability to access all the powers of his splinter-selfs at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then erased himself from existence i'm not sure that it's going to end like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 02-19-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T20:00:42-08:00","id":1051823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WaywardPaladin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1051693#post1051693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legion is capable of ALL the mutant powers. When people die near him, he absorbs their personality. His body manifests a new power appropriate to that person's psyche.<br /> <br /> \u200bHe eventually gains the ability to access all the powers of his splinter-selfs at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true in the comics, we aren't really sure how closely they are sticking with the source material for the show. So for now it can only be used as inspiration for what it has given.<br /> <br /> Also, does he always absorb their personalities in the comics? I thought that only happened when he killed the assassins who killed his step-father. As far as I can remember this lead to his DID state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:59:19-08:00","id":1056753,"title":"","content":"After watching Episode 3, I start to think David in <b>Mage</b> would be from<i> Fangs of Mara</i> Legacy - he has some really creepy Abyssal inhabitants in his Oneiros...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T01:20:08-08:00","id":1057022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046916-legion-tv-series-shows-how-being-mad-one-can-be-great?p=1056753#post1056753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After watching Episode 3, I start to think David in <b>Mage</b> would be from<i> Fangs of Mara</i> Legacy - he has some really creepy Abyssal inhabitants in his Oneiros...</div> </div> </div> </div>Pay no attention to Wimp Lo, we purposely trained him wrong... as a joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions"